{"id":"000VTZ","title":"Interconnected Fog","author":"ruslan","solvedCount":7,"difficulty":2,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-01T19:44:40+00:00","posted":"Heute, 19:46 Uhr","rules":"Interconnected Fog\nby Ruslan\n\nStandard Sudoku\n\nPlace the digits 1-9 exactly once in every row,\ncolumn, and 3x3 box.\n\nFog of War\n\nThe grid is covered in fog. Entering a correct digit\nreveals its cell and the eight surrounding cells,\nincluding any hidden clues. You may enter digits\ninto fog-covered cells if they can be logically\ndetermined. No guessing is required.\n\nThermometers\n\nDigits must strictly increase from the bulb to the\ntip. Thermometers move only orthogonally, cannot\nbranch, and cannot overlap or share cells.\n\nLength Digits\n\nEvery thermometer must contain at least one digit\nequal to its total length in cells, including the\nbulb. For example, a thermometer of length 5 must\ncontain the digit 5.\n\nKropki Dots\n\nWhite dots connect digits that differ by exactly 1.\n\nBlack dots connect digits where one is exactly\ntwice the other.\n\n▶ CLICK TO PLAY IN SUDOKUPAD\n\nEnjoy the puzzle!","solutionCode":"Enter the digits in row 9, reading from left to right.\n\nEnter all 9 digits without spaces or separators.","tags":["Sudoku","Thermometer","Thermo (Variante)","Kropki Pairs (Variante)"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/kbwvrda5fm","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/kbwvrda5fm","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-01T19:44:40+00:00"}